.TH SYSAUD "1" "April 2026" "sysaud 0.1.0" "System Manual"
.SH NAME
sysaud \- Linux system event sound and notification daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysaud
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
.B sysaud
\fBcheck\fR
.PP
.B sysaud
\fBlist-events\fR
.PP
.B sysaud
\fB\-\-json\fR
\fBlist-events\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysaud
is a daemon that listens for system events (via D-Bus, udev, etc.) and fires
sounds, desktop notifications, or custom scripts in response. It is configured
via YAML.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Validate the configuration file.
.TP
\fBlist-events\fR
List all supported events.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-sound\fR
Disable sound playback.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-notify\fR
Disable desktop notifications.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Used with \fBsysaud \-\-json list-events\fR to output events in JSON format.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Specify a custom configuration file path.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration path is
.BR ~/.config/sysaud/config.yaml .
.PP
Example configuration:
.PP
.nf
    daemon:
      lock_app: hyprlock
      log_file: ~/.local/share/sysaud/events.log

    sound:
      enabled: true
      theme: freedesktop
      custom_dir: ~/sounds

    notify:
      enabled: true
      timeout_ms: 4000

    events:
      power.ac-plugged:
        sound: power-plug
        icon: battery-full-charging
        notify: true
      power.ac-unplugged:
        enabled: false
.fi
.SH SUPPORTED EVENTS
.TP
Power events:
power.ac-plugged, power.ac-unplugged, power.battery-low,
power.battery-critical, power.battery-action, power.battery-level
.TP
Network events:
network.wifi-connected, network.network-connected,
network.network-disconnected, network.vpn-connected,
network.vpn-disconnected
.TP
Bluetooth events:
bluetooth.device-connected, bluetooth.device-disconnected,
bluetooth.adapter-on, bluetooth.adapter-off
.TP
USB events:
usb.device-plugged, usb.device-unplugged
.TP
Session events:
session.login, session.screen-locked, session.screen-unlocked,
session.suspend, session.resume
.TP
Display/Disk events:
display.brightness-changed, disk.mounted, disk.unmounted
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
SIGTERM, SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.TP
SIGHUP
Hot reload configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/sysaud/config.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/sysaud/events.log
Event log file (if configured).
